    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it's not even about burnout or finding new hobbies. it just feels like i finished the game. like, i played all the levels, beat the boss, and now the screen is just... blank. there's no more content. i feel like a ghost just going through the motions. it's exhausting to pretend there's a 'next step' when i know there really isn't one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sense of having completed the main quest and facing the blank credits screen is a profound feeling of existential weight. When external goals are met, the internal compass often gets lost, making the day-to-day feel meaningless. This feeling suggests the game itself wasn't the point; the process of becoming, the journey, was what held the energy. You might need to start inventing your own \"content\" now, independent of external milestones.",
      "source": "target",
